  "caveats": [
    "The per-case sample is 23 unique cases out of 693, and every one of them was pulled from a patrol/audit set that the framework selects for difficulty. The corpus mean is plausibly far below this sample's mean, so read the work floor as a floor on a well-behaved corpus rather than a forecast.",
    "The four prose-only readings (Magentic_One/049 twice, Camel/018, Magentic_One/050) are the slowest rows in the sample and the only rows whose source is a report sentence rather than a JSON file. They decide most of the tail; see 'sensitivity' for the estimate computed without them.",
    "One case (Magentic_One/049) was measured at 36.0 and 93.8 minutes under the same config -- a 2.6x spread with no code change. Any single-case point estimate carries that much runway.",
    "The provider is a shared endpoint with no rate-limit contract. If it throttles, throughput falls below every estimate here and the only correction is to lower the worker count and re-measure.",
    "The batch anchors each contain one batch. The audit anchor is dominated by its slowest case, which is a property of that case list, not of the corpus.",
    "Token totals are provider-reported and cover the stages that recorded usage; a case whose envelope lost a stage's usage is excluded rather than counted as cheap."
  ]
